    max difference 2.7e-13 deg; crossings per line with eps_inf > 0: 1: 72
  the flip is a convention: at the flip's kx the straight path w = 1 + i s runs into a branch point of kz(w),
    at s 0.0021 .. 0.823 (every crossing above), in the upper half w plane. The root below it depends on
    which side the path passes, and the straight path is one choice of side.
