  the lateral wave, 42 deg, W 200: |E_r - E_M| / |E_inc(0)| at x = -50 / 0 / 50 is 4.45 / 12.5 / 36.2,
    a growth of 0.0210 per unit x downstream
  the lateral wave, 42 deg, W 300: |E_r - E_M| / |E_inc(0)| at x = -50 / 0 / 50 is 3.22e+03 / 1.04e+04 / 3.4e+04,
    a growth of 0.0236 per unit x downstream
  The growth approaches |Im kx_b(1)| = 0.0250 as W grows. The field at x = 0 is fed from upstream,
    so a wider beam feeds it from further away. Inside the window |E_r/E_inc|^2 is not a reflectance.
  the deformation's direction, 42 deg, W 100. Fingers A and B and a lowered contour at w = 1 share one
    topology, so their agreement tests the integration, not the direction. Only a continuation in w tests
    the direction. A contour lowered to Im kx = -0.035 over kx 0.810 .. 1.198, the root carried along it,
    must match the undeformed real-axis integral at w = 1 + i eta while kx_b(w) is above the axis (eta > s_c
    = 0.0183). At eta 0.02 / 0.025 / 0.03 the relative gap is 4e-14 / 3e-14 / 3e-14. Control: the same contour
    raised to Im kx = +0.035 passes above kx_b(w) and misses by 0.35 / 0.41 / 0.52.
    Carried from eta 0.03 to 0 in 31 steps, kx_b(1 + i eta) stays above the lowered contour (least clearance
    0.0100; Re inside the detour: yes), so the integral is analytic in eta all the way (largest root
    turn per node 0.5 deg). At eta = 0 it gives E_r: |E_low - E_r| / |E_r - E_M| = 5e-15.

3. margin -- past the c = 2 edge, at ratio 2.107 (44.5 deg at g 0.05), high side: |E_r - E_M| / |E_inc| at x = 0
  The tip term goes as exp((W/2)^2 (Im^2 - (kx0 - Re)^2)), kx_b(1) = Re + i Im ("tip"). For weak gain that is
  exp(-(rho^2 - 1) (W/L_g)^2 / 4) ("formula"), with the gain length L_g = 2 sqrt(Re eps) / (k0 |Im eps|).
  Lines: wc 1, gam 0.1, pinned to eps(1) = 1 - i g. A row whose tip weight is below exp(-690) is skipped:
  the deviation is below the double range. Cauchy and refine as in section 2; past 1e-8 prints as unreliable.
