4. far flip -- beams between Maystre's step and a far fixed-kx flip: the beam goes to Maystre's value
  B uses eps(1) alone. A runs along the line's own trajectory kx_b(1 + i s). A's real-axis part carries the
  fixed-kx causal kernel over the beam centre ("step"), and its finger cancels that. So |A - B| is read
  against "A size", the sum of the sizes of A's terms, which sets A's round-off. "overflow": the Gaussian
  on the trajectory leaves the double range; "A unresolved": past 1e-10 of A size. refine as in section 2.
