5. top hat -- a field e^{i k0 x} on |x| < L/2 onto the centred line (g 0.05): |E_r - E_M| / |E_inc| at x = 0
  Its spectrum is entire and of exponential type, so on the finger it weighs up to exp(|Im kx_b(1)| L/2),
  at any angle. Its upstream edge seeds a lateral wave that grows over L/2 before it reaches x = 0.
  Unlike a Gaussian's, its spectrum is not small at the mirror point -kx_b(1), which the contour passes
  above. By symmetry that finger is finger B with a(k) replaced by a(-k); "mirror" is its share. The
  Gaussian column is section 2's deviation at W = L. Cauchy and refine as in section 2, on the sum.
